Therefore, our linear function must be  $y=\dfrac{3}{2}x-8$. Inputting $x=4t-2$ (we can get $x$ by adding 2 to the $x$-coordinate of the starting point) we get the final answer of $y=\dfrac{3}{2}(4t-2)$ or $y=\boxed{6t-3}$. </think><answer> 6t-3 </answer>

